# .trivyignore — CVE suppression file for ClearLedger
#
# PURPOSE: Explicitly suppress CVEs that have been reviewed and accepted.
#          Each entry requires a documented justification.
#          This file is code-reviewed and committed to Git — it is an
#          explicit decision, not a silent suppression.
#
# RULE: Never add a CVE here to make a build go green without review.
#       If you are adding a CVE, the PR description must include:
#         - Why the CVE does not apply or is not exploitable in this context
#         - Who approved the risk acceptance
#         - The date it was reviewed and when to re-evaluate
#
# FORMAT:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # justification
#
# EXAMPLE (remove and replace with real entries as needed):
#
# CVE-2023-12345  # only exploitable via local console access — our containers
#                  # have no console. Reviewed 2026-01-15. Re-evaluate 2026-07-15.
#                  # Approved by: platform-lead
#
# When a fix becomes available, remove the entry and let Trivy catch the
# updated version requirement naturally.
